== Stage 3 ==
;6 July 2026 – [[Granollers]] to [[Les Angles, Pyrénées-Orientales|Les Angles]], {{convert|195.9|km|abbr=on}}

The third stage of the race took riders northwards into [[France]] and into the [[Pyrenees]], on a {{convert|195.9|km|abbr=on}} mountainous course from [[Granollers]] to [[Les Angles, Pyrénées-Orientales|Les Angles]]. The stage featured four categorised climbs, including the first-category Col de Toses (9.3&nbsp;km at an average gradient of 6.5%) and the third-category finish to Les Angles (1.7&nbsp;km at an average gradient of 6.5%).<ref>{{Cite web |title=Stage 3 - Granollers > Les Angles - Tour de France 2026 |url=https://www.letour.fr/en/stage-3 |access-date=4 July 2026 |website=www.letour.fr |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite book |title=2026 Tour de France Roadbook |publisher=Amaury Sport Organisation |pages=34, 36}}</ref> Owing to [[Wildfire|wildfires]] in the [[Pyrénées-Orientales]] department, spectators were discouraged from attending the race in France, with no spectators at the finish.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-07-06 |title=Tour de France 2026: Fans urged not to attend end of third stage because of wildfires |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/cycling/articles/c77yy3dmddxo |access-date=2026-07-06 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref>

On the stage, it took {{convert|65|km|abbr=on}} for a breakaway to be formed, after numerous attacks were chased down by {{UCI team code|UEX|2026|nolink=y}} and {{UCI team code|TVL men|2026|nolink=y}}. 20 riders were in the breakaway included Pedersen and [[Alex Baudin]] ({{UCI team code|EFE|2026}}). Pedersen won the intermediate sprints, and Baudin took the points of the mountains classification at the Col de Toses. As {{UCI team code|UEX|2026|nolink=y}} increased the pace, the break reduced in size to 6 riders approaching the Col de la Calvaire. Baudin broke free, taking more mountain points at the top of the Col, but was swallowed by the peloton shortly after.<ref name="CN-3" /><ref name=":5">{{Cite news |last=Whittle |first=Jeremy |date=2026-07-06 |title=Pogacar rises above wildfire restrictions to take yellow jersey in deserted Les Angles |url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/jul/06/pogacar-rises-above-wildfire-restrictions-to-take-yellow-jersey-in-deserted-les-angles |access-date=2026-07-10 |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref>

On the final climb to Les Angles, {{UCI team code|UEX|2026|nolink=y}} set a fast pace, with del Toro attacking with 300 metres remaining to set up an attack by Pogačar. Pogačar crossed the line 2 seconds ahead of Vingegaard, [[Richard Carapaz]] ({{UCI team code|EFE|2026|nolink=y}}) and [[Paul Seixas]] ({{UCI team code|DCT|2026|nolink=}}) with Pogačar taking the yellow jersey off Vingegaard as a result. Baudin took the polka dot jersey of the mountains classification, and del Toro maintained their lead in the young rider classification. Pogačar called the hot weather a "logistical nightmare", owing to the constant need for water bottles from the team car.<ref name="CN-3" /><ref name=":5" />

