== Stage 5 ==
;8 July 2026 – [[Lannemezan]] to [[Pau, Pyrénées-Atlantiques|Pau]], {{convert|158.3|km|abbr=on}}
[[File:Olav Kooij on the podium at the presentation ceremony for Stage 5 of the 2026 Tour de France.jpg|thumb|Stage winner [[Olav Kooij]] ({{UCI team code|DCT|2026|nolink=}}), pictured prior to the start of the stage]]
The fifth stage of the race took riders from [[Lannemezan]] to [[Pau, Pyrénées-Atlantiques|Pau]] on a flat course, with one third-category climb on the {{convert|158.3|km|abbr=on}} route.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Stage 5 - Lannemezan > Pau - Tour de France 2026 |url=https://www.letour.fr/en/stage-5 |access-date=4 July 2026 |website=www.letour.fr |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite book |title=2026 Tour de France Roadbook |publisher=Amaury Sport Organisation |pages=52, 54}}</ref>

Owing to the heat and the expected sprint finish, [[Baptiste Veistroffer]] ({{UCI team code|LOI|2026|nolink=}}) was the lone breakaway rider for much of the day, with a maximum lead of 4 minutes. At the intermediate sprint, [[Max Kanter]] ({{UCI team code|XAT|2026|nolink=}}) beat Pedersen, Girmay and Philipsen. Veistroffer was caught with around {{convert|14|km|abbr=on}} remaining. Approaching the finish, a crash occurred with {{convert|5.5|km|abbr=on}} to go – no {{abbr|GC|general classification}} riders or contenders for the sprint finish were involved. A reduced group of 20 riders headed for a sprint finish, with [[Olav Kooij]] ({{UCI team code|DCT|2026|nolink=y}}) beating Kanter and [[Tim Merlier]] ({{UCI team code|SOQ|2026|nolink=}}) to take his first stage win at the Tour.<ref name=":8">{{Cite web |last=Ostanek |first=Dani |last2= |first2= |date=2026-07-08 |title=Tour de France: Olav Kooij shines in debut with victory on stage 5 in Pau |url=https://www.cyclingnews.com/pro-cycling/racing/tour-de-france-olav-kooij-shines-in-debut-with-victory-on-stage-5-in-pau/ |access-date=2026-07-10 |website=Cyclingnews |language=en}}</ref><ref name=":9">{{Cite news |last=Whittle |first=Jeremy |date=2026-07-08 |title=Olav Kooij claims Tour de France stage five with Tourmalet test looming large |url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/jul/08/olav-kooij-claims-tour-de-france-stage-five-with-tourmalet-test-looming-large |access-date=2026-07-10 |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref> Pedersen finished 7th in the green jersey, extending their lead in the points classification. Træen remained in the yellow jersey and Baudin remained in the polka dot jersey of the mountains classification after an uneventful day for the peloton.<ref name=":8" /><ref name=":9" />

